  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "My brethren, have not the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Lord of glory, with respect of persons.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For if there come unto your assembly a man with a gold ring, in goodly apparel, and there come in also a poor man in vile raiment;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And ye have respect to him that weareth the gay clothing, and say unto him, Sit thou here in a good place; and say to the poor, Stand thou there, or sit here under my footstool:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Are ye not then partial in yourselves, and are become judges of evil thoughts?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Hearken, my beloved brethren, Hath not God chosen the poor of this world rich in faith, and heirs of the kingdom which he hath promised to them that love him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "But ye have despised the poor. Do not rich men oppress you, and draw you before the judgment seats?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Do not they blaspheme that worthy name by the which ye are called?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "If ye fulfil the royal law according to the scripture, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself, ye do well:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "But if ye have respect to persons, ye commit sin, and are convinced of the law as transgressors.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For whosoever shall keep the whole law, and yet offend in one point, he is guilty of all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For he that said, Do not commit adultery, said also, Do not kill. Now if thou commit no adultery, yet if thou kill, thou art become a transgressor of the law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "So speak ye, and so do, as they that shall be judged by the law of liberty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For he shall have judgment without mercy, that hath shewed no mercy; and mercy rejoiceth against judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "What doth it profit, my brethren, though a man say he hath faith, and have not works? can faith save him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "If a brother or sister be naked, and destitute of daily food,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And one of you say unto them, Depart in peace, be ye warmed and filled; notwithstanding ye give them not those things which are needful to the body; what doth it profit?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Yea, a man may say, Thou hast faith, and I have works: shew me thy faith without thy works, and I will shew thee my faith by my works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "But wilt thou know, O vain man, that faith without works is dead?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Was not Abraham our father justified by works, when he had offered Isaac his son upon the altar?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Seest thou how faith wrought with his works, and by works was faith made perfect?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "And the scripture was fulfilled which saith, Abraham believed God, and it was imputed unto him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Ye see then how that by works a man is justified, and not by faith only.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Likewise also was not Rahab the harlot justified by works, when she had received the messengers, and had sent them out another way?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:2:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "For as the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without works is dead also.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 2:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:2:26"
      }
    }
  ],
